2. Fragment wiring change

File:

android-sdk-v5-sample/src/main/java/dji/sampleV5/aircraft/pages/VirtualStickFragment.kt

Inside:
private fun initBtnClickListener()


binding?.btnExecuteCommand?.setOnClickListener {
    val command = binding?.commandInput?.text.toString().trim().lowercase()

    if (command == "forward") {
        virtualStickVM.moveForwardTwoSeconds()
    } else {
        ToastUtils.showToast("Unknown command: $command")
    }
}


Purpose:

When you press "Execute Command",
the app reads the text from command_input.

If the text is "forward",
it calls virtualStickVM.moveForwardTwoSeconds().

Important:

The drone does not understand the word "forward".
Your Android app translates "forward" into a Virtual Stick command.


3. VirtualStickVM command function

File:

android-sdk-v5-sample/src/main/java/dji/sampleV5/aircraft/models/VirtualStickVM.kt

We added this function:

fun moveForwardTwoSeconds() {
    val param = VirtualStickFlightControlParam().apply {
        rollPitchCoordinateSystem = FlightCoordinateSystem.BODY
        verticalControlMode = VerticalControlMode.VELOCITY
        yawControlMode = YawControlMode.ANGULAR_VELOCITY
        rollPitchControlMode = RollPitchControlMode.ANGLE

        pitch = 2.0
        roll = 0.0
        yaw = 0.0
        verticalThrottle = 0.0
    }

    sendVirtualStickAdvancedParam(param)

    android.os.Handler(android.os.Looper.getMainLooper()).postDelayed({
        param.pitch = 0.0
        sendVirtualStickAdvancedParam(param)
    }, 2000)
}

Purpose:

Creates a VirtualStickFlightControlParam.
Sets pitch = 2.0.
Sends it to the drone.
Waits 2 seconds.
Sets pitch back to 0.0.
Sends the zero command to stop movement.



